## NestJS Features

### Modules

NestJS applications are organized into modules. Each module encapsulates:

- **Controllers**: Handle HTTP requests
- **Providers**: Services, repositories, factories, etc.
- **Imports**: Other modules used by this module
- **Exports**: Features this module provides to other modules

```typescript
import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ExampleController } from './example.controller';
import { ExampleService } from './example.service';

@Module({
  imports: [],
  controllers: [ExampleController],
  providers: [ExampleService],
  exports: [ExampleService],
})
export class ExampleModule {}
```

### Controllers

Controllers handle HTTP requests and define API endpoints:

```typescript
import { Controller, Get, Post, Body, Param } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ExampleService } from './example.service';

@Controller('examples')
export class ExampleController {
  constructor(private readonly exampleService: ExampleService) {}

  @Get()
  findAll() {
    return this.exampleService.findAll();
  }

  @Get(':id')
  findOne(@Param('id') id: string) {
    return this.exampleService.findOne(id);
  }

  @Post()
  create(@Body() createExampleDto: CreateExampleDto) {
    return this.exampleService.create(createExampleDto);
  }
}
```

### Providers

Providers are services that can be injected into controllers and other providers:

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';

@Injectable()
export class ExampleService {
  private examples: Example[] = [];

  findAll(): Example[] {
    return this.examples;
  }

  findOne(id: string): Example {
    return this.examples.find(example => example.id === id);
  }

  create(createExampleDto: CreateExampleDto): Example {
    const example = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...createExampleDto };
    this.examples.push(example);
    return example;
  }
}
```

### Dependency Injection

NestJS has a powerful dependency injection system:

```typescript
// Provider
@Injectable()
export class DatabaseService {
  constructor(private readonly configService: ConfigService) {}
  
  connect() {
    const host = this.configService.get('DB_HOST');
    // Connect to database
  }
}

// Controller using provider
@Controller('database')
export class DatabaseController {
  constructor(private readonly databaseService: DatabaseService) {}
  
  @Get('connect')
  connect() {
    this.databaseService.connect();
    return { status: 'connected' };
  }
}
```

